 * Get details for a specific comment (BBS: comments table).
 *
 * This API allows users to fetch all available information for one specific
 * comment within the context of a post. The identifiers ('postId' for the
 * parent thread, 'id' for the comment itself) ensure accuracy in comment
 * threading and navigation. The operation returns comment content, author and
 * timestamp details, metadata, and relations (such as parent reply or nested
 * replies).
 *
 * The endpoint supports use cases like displaying a reply in context, enabling
 * further replies, or feeding comment moderation workflows. If a comment is not
 * found or the identifiers do not match, the API returns a not-found error.
 * Related endpoints include comment listing (PATCH), creation (POST), updating
 * (PUT), and deletion (DELETE).
 *
 * @param props.connection
 * @param props.postId The unique post to which the comment belongs.
 * @param props.id The specific comment identifier to retrieve.
 * @path /bbs/posts/:postId/comments/:id
 * @autobe Generated by AutoBE - https://github.com/wrtnlabs/autobe
 */
