/**
 * Comprehensive test: comment deletion (soft delete) by author, moderator/administrator, and unauthorized user.
 *
 * Validates the following:
 * 1. Author can soft delete their own comment (deleted_at set)
 * 2. Moderator can delete comments by any user
 * 3. Unrelated user is denied deletion (permission error)
 * 4. Deletion is not idempotent (repeat deletion yields error or no-op)
 * 5. Deleting a non-existent comment returns correct error
 * 6. Deleted comment cannot be interacted with by regular users
 *
 * **Steps:**
 * 1. Create test users (author, moderator, unrelated)
 * 2. Author creates a post
 * 3. Author comments on the post
 * 4. Author soft deletes own comment
 * 5. Moderator creates fresh comment and deletes it
 * 6. Unrelated user attempts comment deletion (denied)
 * 7. Attempt to re-delete deleted comment (should error/no-op)
